        "theme":  "Agents",
        "summary":  "Cohere Health built Cohere Policy Studio on Amazon Bedrock AgentCore to automate conversion of clinical prior-authorization policies from static documents into structured, machine-readable formats. The implementation cut policy digitization time by 30 percent and compressed full agent deployment timelines from 3-4 months to 2-6 weeks through reusable container images, AgentCore Gateway for unified tool access, and modular skills frameworks. Multi-tenant security isolation and human-in-the-loop workflows ensure regulatory compliance and clinical oversight throughout.",
        "execSummary":  "Cohere Health\u0027s deployment demonstrates that agentic AI architectures are now production-viable in one of the most regulated sectors ΓÇö healthcare prior authorization ΓÇö with measurable operational results: 30% faster policy processing and 6-8 week deployment cycles replacing multi-month ones. For enterprise leaders evaluating AI agent platforms, this case validates Amazon Bedrock AgentCore as a credible enterprise-grade orchestration layer with built-in multi-tenancy and gateway controls that address key security and compliance objections. The human-in-the-loop design is the critical architectural choice that keeps clinical liability manageable ΓÇö a pattern directly transferable to other high-stakes enterprise workflows. Caveat: this is an AWS-authored case study; independent audit of the 30% efficiency claim is not available.",
        "vendorLean":  "AWS ΓÇö AWS-published case study promoting Bedrock AgentCore; Cohere Health outcomes presented without independent verification.",
