        "date":  "2026-08-07",
        "theme":  "Agents",
        "summary":  "The TReNDS Center built an agentic AI system using Amazon Bedrock and the Strands Agents SDK that autonomously investigates production errors by analyzing stack traces, retrieving relevant source code from GitHub, and delivering structured root-cause analysis reports to engineering teams. The architecture combines CloudWatch subscription filters, AWS Lambda, and foundation models to compress error investigation time from 15-30 minutes to under 60 seconds. The agent autonomously selects diagnostic tools and code files to examine, replicating the decision-making pattern of an experienced engineer.",
        "execSummary":  "Compressing production error diagnosis from 30 minutes to under 60 seconds with an autonomous agent is a credible, quantifiable outcome that support and engineering operations leaders can benchmark directly against their own incident-response costs. This use case sits at the intersection of AI agents and IT support automation ΓÇö a direct analog for customer-support AI that escalates, investigates, and resolves issues without waiting for human triage. For leaders building AI-augmented operations centers, the Strands Agents SDK + Bedrock combination shown here is a replicable reference architecture. Key caveat: accuracy of automated root-cause analysis in novel failure modes is not quantified; human review thresholds should be defined before full autonomy is granted.",
