        "execSummary":  "Enterprise AI agent adoption is accelerating faster than most strategic plans anticipated: the average Salesforce customer now runs 13 agents ΓÇö up from 5 in early 2025 ΓÇö and spins up a new one in under two days. For senior leaders, the implication is that the window to establish governance, orchestration standards, and cost controls is narrowing rapidly. Organizations that treat agent deployment as purely a speed-and-scale win, without investing in oversight frameworks, risk compounding the cost and security problems already surfacing across the industry. The key caveat: deployment volume is rising faster than measurable business value, suggesting depth of use ΓÇö not just breadth ΓÇö is the missing ingredient.",
