        "theme":  "Strategy",
        "summary":  "CIOs are redesigning governance structures to balance accelerating AI adoption with appropriate risk management. Experts discuss strategies including structurally separating oversight and adoption teams and using multi-level maturity models for scaling AI safely. The article explores how IT leaders avoid both over-restriction that stifles value and under-governance that creates enterprise risk.",
        "execSummary":  "The central tension for enterprise AI leadership in 2026 is not whether to adopt AI but how to govern it without choking value creation. CIOs who are winning are separating the teams responsible for AI oversight from those driving adoption ΓÇö preventing the governance function from becoming a bottleneck. For customer-support leaders, this translates directly: agentic AI in service operations needs a dedicated risk track, not ad hoc review. The implication to watch is that governance maturity is becoming a competitive differentiator, not just a compliance checkbox.",
