        "theme":  "Strategy",
        "summary":  "The article examines six critical strategic decisions CIOs face in balancing competing organizational priorities, including IT foundation versus growth investments, innovation versus operational resilience, and speed versus organizational readiness. AI has intensified these traditional trade-offs by adding escalating cost pressures and capability expectations simultaneously. The piece emphasizes that miscalibrating any one of these trade-offs can compound failures across the others.",
        "execSummary":  "AI has turned long-standing CIO trade-offs into high-stakes decisions with faster feedback loops: misjudging the balance between AI cost investment and operational stability can now derail a quarter\u0027s results, not just a planning cycle. For senior leaders, the most decision-critical tension is speed versus organizational readiness ΓÇö deploying AI faster than the workforce and governance structures can absorb it is a documented failure mode. Customer-support leaders face this acutely when deploying agentic AI: the technology can be live in days, but the process redesign, training, and escalation frameworks take months. The key implication is that sequencing ΓÇö not just selection ΓÇö of AI investments is what separates leaders from laggards.",
