        "source":  "CIO Dive",
        "url":  "https://www.ciodive.com/news/agentic-productivity-c-suite-value/826999/",
        "date":  "2026-08-04",
        "theme":  "Agents",
        "summary":  "Accenture research shows agentic AI is delivering strong productivity gains and employee satisfaction, but fewer organizations are achieving measurable business value. Only 23% of companies reported reportable business value in July 2026, down from 32% earlier in the year. The decline suggests that widespread but shallow AI implementations fail to drive enterprise-level financial impact.",
        "execSummary":  "The productivity-to-value gap in agentic AI is widening, not closing: Accenture data shows business value realization has dropped from 32% to 23% of enterprises even as adoption accelerates. For senior leaders, this is the clearest signal yet that agent deployment without process redesign and outcome accountability produces activity, not results. The implication for customer-support leaders is direct ΓÇö deploying agents that handle volume without measurably improving resolution rates, cost-per-contact, or customer satisfaction scores will not survive CFO scrutiny. The key caveat to watch is whether organizations are measuring the right outcomes; many may be capturing productivity metrics (handle time, deflection) while missing the financial value metrics boards care about.",
