        "date":  "2026-08-04",
        "theme":  "Enterprise",
        "summary":  "A WitnessAI survey found that over 40% of enterprises experienced AI-related security incidents costing $2 million or more annually. Most strikingly, IT and infrastructure departments ΓÇö the very teams responsible for AI governance ΓÇö are also the largest sources of unsanctioned shadow AI activity. The research reveals a critical gap between adoption speed and security risk management across enterprise organizations.",
        "execSummary":  "The function responsible for AI governance is simultaneously the largest source of shadow AI risk ΓÇö a contradiction that undermines enterprise AI security from the inside. For senior leaders, this finding demands that AI governance frameworks include self-auditing mechanisms for IT and infrastructure teams, not just business units. The $2M+ incident cost threshold affects more than 40% of enterprises, making this a material financial risk that belongs in ERM and board reporting. The caveat: WitnessAI is a vendor with products designed to address shadow AI, so scope and framing of the survey should be verified against independent research before driving major policy changes.",
