        "summary":  "The article surveys six AI-powered development environments ΓÇö GitHub Copilot, Google Antigravity, JetBrains Air, Kiro, Zed, and Zenflow ΓÇö that assist developers with code generation and agent-based automation. Development practices have shifted from manual coding to reviewing AI-generated code, with approaches ranging from vibe coding to specification-driven development. Each tool offers distinct features, model support, and workflow capabilities for different development team needs.",
        "execSummary":  "The AI-powered development environment market has matured to a point where enterprise technology leaders must now make a deliberate platform choice, not just a tool add-on decision ΓÇö six distinct products with different architectural philosophies are competing for developer workflow ownership. For enterprise IT and engineering leaders, the strategic implication is that which platform wins internally will shape developer productivity, security posture, and vendor lock-in for years. The shift from \u0027AI assists coding\u0027 to \u0027developers review AI output\u0027 is a fundamental change in how software quality is maintained and how IP and security risk should be governed. The key caveat: the landscape is moving fast and today\u0027s comparison may be outdated within a product cycle.",
